    "memoEntities": {
      "memo_legend": {
        "id": "memo_legend",
        "value": "PagePass MVP target ERD\n\nBlue: auth    Green: family\nCyan: device  Amber: app policy\nRed: time     Purple: reading/OCR\nGray: system and operations\n\nTarget model, not the current migration state.\nStandalone design artifact.",
        "ui": {
          "x": 31.8182,
          "y": 5590.9091,
          "zIndex": 100,
          "width": 2500,
          "height": 850,
          "color": "#176B5B"
        },
        "meta": {
          "updateAt": 1785182543290,
          "createAt": 1784323200000
        }
      },
      "memo_constraints": {
        "id": "memo_constraints",
        "value": "PostgreSQL and service invariants\n\n1. FKs model ownership and lifecycle only.\n2. Every child-owned row has a child_profile_id ownership FK.\n3. Secondary references use globally unique UUIDs, not composite child-scoped FKs.\n4. The API validates that secondary references belong to the same child inside one transaction.\n5. Actor, source, uploader, replacement, supersession, and recipient IDs are historical metadata, intentionally not FKs.\n6. One active device per child:\n   UNIQUE(child_profile_id) WHERE status = 'active'.\n7. One unsettled Earned Time session per child:\n   UNIQUE(child_profile_id) WHERE state IN\n   ('prepared','active','settlement_pending').\n8. One pending app request per managed app:\n   UNIQUE(child_profile_id, managed_app_id)\n   WHERE status = 'pending'.\n9. credit_ledger_entries and submission_reviews are append-only.\n10. Ledger append and child_credit_balances projection update occur in one transaction.\n11. Approved review and reading_reward ledger append occur in one transaction.\n12. Each positive-consumption settled Earned Time session maps to one session_spend ledger row; a zero-second stop records only the idempotent session result.\n13. Exactly one notification recipient reference is present.\n14. At most one audit actor reference is present; system events may have none.\n15. profile_media_id and cover/evidence media must exist, belong to the same child, and have the correct kind.\n16. Pairing expires after 5 minutes and is single-use; a new session invalidates the old open session.\n17. Opaque app tokens, APNs tokens, and credentials never enter logs or audit payloads.\n18. Domain records are archived or revoked; hard delete is reserved for retention jobs.\n19. Exactly one media uploader reference is present: Parent or child device.\n20. Review and session state checks remain database CHECK constraints where practical.\n21. An AFTER INSERT trigger creates child_credit_balances for every child_profile during rolling deploys.\n22. Earned Time billing uses server-authoritative activation and final receipt timestamps, capped at expiry.\n23. A new start atomically settles an expired active session before evaluating the next reservation.\n24. Child setup completion retires old active devices and promotes one verified pending device in one transaction.\n25. Device replacement is rejected while the outgoing device has a nonexpired active Earned Time session.",
        "ui": {
          "x": 1731.8182,
          "y": 5718.1818,
          "zIndex": 101,
          "width": 2500,
          "height": 2200,
          "color": "#C84949"
        },
        "meta": {
          "updateAt": 1785182543290,
          "createAt": 1784323200000
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
